Description: add a Makefile and make the launcher safe
 Adds a Makefile that assembles the intro with nasm, compresses it with
 gzip -n (reproducible) and writes the self-extracting launcher under the
 package name.
 .
 The upstream stub extracted the ELF to the fixed path /tmp/L: another user
 (or another intro using the same trick) could not run it at the same time,
 and the predictable name allowed symlink attacks. The stub is now a real
 shell script (with a shebang) that extracts the intro into a private
 mktemp directory, removed on exit. It exits with 0: the intro itself
 always ends with exit status 4.
